From a09d16453bb256d9c9b557188e0454a5c979abeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:01:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(reframe): no blurred-copy fill; analyse 4K sources
 at a usable resolution

Root cause #4 of clip1.mp4 (handoff/quality-clip1/ROOT_CAUSE.md):
- the fit layout filled the top and bottom thirds with a blurred, enlarged
  copy of the picture; on wide crowd shots two thirds of every frame was
  smeared imagery;
- shots came out "no_subject" because analysis decodes at 480 px: a 4K
  frame shrinks 8x and a seated person's face is ~25 px for the detector.

media/fit_pad.py, FIT_PAD (default "blur" = byte-identical filters until
Luffy approves, Sanji Q15): "ambient" fills the bars with the frame's
average colour, darkened and desaturated (no imagery). Used by the EDL
compositor backdrop and reframing.build_full_frame_filter / crop+fit graph.

REFRAME_HIRES_PROBE (default off): sources >= 2560 px wide are analysed at
960 px instead of 480; 1080p sources unchanged. The reframe cache records
the probe mode and is not reused across modes.

Evidence (same 141-199 s window, Steps 1+2 on):
handoff/quality-clip1/step2/ - the clip is now sharp 4K crops of the
streamer, no blur; known limit: the crop hides the stage screen he reacts
to (Step 3's job). Forced-fit proof of the ambient pad: step2/fit_pad_proof.
Tests: test_fit_pad 7/7; reframe/render suites 203 passed, 5 failed - all 5
fail identically on 996d074 (Windows drawtext paths, editor export file lock).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
